# Read by Docker (BuildKit, the default builder) for worker/Dockerfile. The build context is the REPO ROOT (docker-compose.yml:
# context "..", `docker build -f worker/Dockerfile .`), so the paths here start at the repo root. A plain worker/.dockerignore is
# not read for that build; it holds the same list for a build whose context is worker/.
# Only what the Dockerfile copies is sent to the builder (two folders and the two price files). The rest of the repo (web/, the
# other tools/, .git, any .env) is not.
*
!worker
!typesafe/photo_train
!tools/price_lookup.py
!tools/merimen-part-prices-data.md
# local secrets, caches and tests: not needed to run the worker
**/.env
**/.env.*
!worker/.env.example
**/*.key
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules
**/.venv*
**/*.log
worker/tests
worker/cdp.test.mjs
# a WORKER_STATE that someone pointed inside worker/: Chrome profiles (logged-in sessions), downloaded case files, model weights
worker/state
worker/.state
worker/var
worker/files
worker/chrome
worker/photo-model
worker/NEED_LOGIN
# the photo model's weights and training data never go into the image (the worker downloads production/ itself)
typesafe/photo_train/models
typesafe/photo_train/data
typesafe/photo_train/*.txt
typesafe/photo_train/*.pt
